-> Reference: the three loop forms. `loop <var> over <array> get
-> <result>` is bounded by the array's length. `loop <var> get <result>
-> { }` (no `over`) enumerates a variable's own finite domain instead.
-> `loop get <result> { }` (no variable) has no built-in bound — it runs
-> until an explicit `break`. `yield` collects values into the result in
-> any of them.
prices = [12, 45, 8, 99, 3]
loop p over prices get affordable {
    if p < 50 {
        yield p
    }
}
assert affordable = [12, 45, 8, 3]

n ∈ { 1, 2, 3 }
loop n get doubled {
    yield n * 2
}
assert doubled = [2, 4, 6]

should_stop = true
loop get done {
    if should_stop {
        break
    }
    yield 1
}
assert done = []
